Feature: Define Target User/Customer Outcome
  As a cross-functional squad member
  I want to translate our chosen JTBD into a clear, measurable outcome
  So that we have specific guidance for our delivery focus and success criteria

  Background:
    Given a high-opportunity JTBD has been identified and selected
    And cross-functional squad members are aligned on the JTBD priority
    And business/customer proxies are available for outcome validation
    And measurement capabilities exist to track outcome achievement

  @smart-outcomes @measurable-targets
  Scenario: Draft SMART outcome statement collaboratively
    Given the squad has selected a top-scoring JTBD as their focus
    When they collaboratively draft an outcome statement
    Then the outcome follows SMART criteria (Specific, Measurable, Achievable, Relevant, Time-bound)
    And the outcome directly addresses the selected JTBD
    And quantitative success thresholds are clearly defined
    And the timeline for achievement is realistic and specified
    And all squad members contribute to and understand the outcome statement

  @stakeholder-validation @consensus-building
  Scenario: Validate outcome with business and customer proxies
    Given a SMART outcome statement has been drafted
    When the squad presents the outcome to business/customer proxies
    Then business stakeholders confirm the outcome aligns with strategic objectives
    And customer proxies validate that achievement will solve real user problems
    And any concerns or modifications are addressed collaboratively
    And final consensus is reached on the outcome statement
    And all parties sign off on the target outcome to guide work

  @success-metrics @measurement-framework
  Scenario: Define explicit, measurable success criteria
    Given a validated outcome statement exists
    When the squad defines success criteria and metrics
    Then 2-3 explicit, measurable success criteria are established
    And each criterion directly indicates outcome achievement
    And measurement methods and data sources are identified
    And baseline measurements are captured where possible
    And success thresholds are realistic yet ambitious
    And tracking cadence and responsibility are assigned

  @real-world-application @sales-dashboard-outcome
  Scenario: Define outcome for sales dashboard JTBD
    Given the squad selected "Help sales leaders get accurate pipeline insights in real-time" as their JTBD
    When they translate this JTBD into a measurable outcome
    Then they define "95% of sales users can answer their top 3 pipeline questions in under 30 seconds"
    And the outcome is specific about user percentage and time threshold
    And "top 3 pipeline questions" are explicitly identified and documented
    And measurement approach for user success rate and response time is established
    And sales leadership validates this outcome addresses their core need

  @onboarding-example @user-activation
  Scenario: Define outcome for user onboarding JTBD  
    Given the squad selected "increase onboarding success" as their JTBD with Opportunity Score 14
    When they define the target outcome
    Then they specify "80% of new users launch a project in less than 3 minutes"
    And the outcome includes specific user percentage and time constraint
    And "launch a project" action is clearly defined and measurable
    And tracking mechanisms for new user behavior are established
    And the 3-minute threshold is validated as meaningful for user success

  @outcome-refinement @iterative-improvement
  Scenario: Refine outcome statement based on stakeholder feedback
    Given an initial outcome statement has been drafted
    And feedback has been gathered from business/customer proxies
    When refinements are needed to improve clarity or achievability
    Then the squad collaboratively updates the outcome statement
    And changes are validated with all stakeholders
    And rationale for modifications is documented
    And the final outcome maintains SMART characteristics
    And team consensus is maintained throughout refinement process

  @anti-pattern @vague-outcomes
  Scenario: Prevent vague or unmeasurable outcome statements
    Given the squad is defining their target outcome
    When outcome statements are being evaluated
    Then vague terms like "improve user experience" are rejected
    And qualitative-only outcomes without metrics are refined
    And outcomes without clear success thresholds are strengthened
    And time-bound elements are added to open-ended statements
    And the final outcome enables clear success/failure determination
